## This file is used by Android Studio / Gradle (sdk.dir is usually auto-added).
## Copy to local.properties and set sdk.dir + orchestrator.ws.

## Hosted demo (physical watch over the internet) — the Amazon API Gateway
## WebSocket endpoint printed by `cdk deploy`:
orchestrator.ws=wss://xxxxxxxx.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/care

## Local laptop on same Wi-Fi as the watch — replace with your LAN IP:
## orchestrator.ws=ws://192.168.1.42:3001/care
## Windows Mobile Hotspot gateway (typical):
## orchestrator.ws=ws://192.168.137.1:3001/care
## Emulator builds can omit this line (defaults to ws://10.0.2.2:3001/care).
## Legacy .../ws URLs are rewritten to /care by the watch client.
## After changing this file: Gradle sync + rebuild/reinstall the APK.

## ---- Ally (deployed API) ----
## HTTPS URL from `cdk deploy` output ApiUrl, and the device key printed by ally/scripts/put_secrets.py
## ally.api=https://xxxxxxxx.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com
## ally.deviceKey=paste-device-key-here
